# Only what the image needs. Local secrets, databases, virtualenvs and build output stay out:
# an image is a file people copy around (see deploy/internal/make-bundle.sh).
.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env*.example
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/data/
# ...except the vendored Shelf-Life catalogue, which is code data, not a local database.
!backend/data/shelf-life
!backend/data/shelf-life/**
# ...and the Make it safe recipes (services/make_safe.py), sourced vendor data the service reads.
!backend/data/make_safe_recipes.json
# ...and the list of CDN, API, ad and tracking hosts the front page leaves out of its rows of names (services/infra_hosts.py).
!backend/data/infrastructure_hosts.json
# ...and the quantum threat board's reviewed dataset (services/threat_board.py), which Morrow's quantum year is read from.
!backend/data/threat-board
!backend/data/threat-board/**
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/*.log
**/*.err
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.pem
**/*.key
